    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="daily-protein-needs">How Much Protein You Really Need</h2>
  <p>Protein needs vary dramatically based on your body weight and goals:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Goal / Category</th><th scope="col">Daily intake</th><th scope="col">Grams per kg body weight</th><th scope="col">Calories from 150g protein</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Sedentary adult (RDA)</td><td>Prevent deficiency</td><td>0.8 g</td><td>600 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>General health</td><td>Maintenance</td><td>1.0–1.2 g</td><td>600–720 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Recomposition</td><td>Muscle preservation</td><td>1.2–1.6 g</td><td>720–960 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Weight loss</td><td>Preserve muscle in deficit</td><td>1.6–2.2 g</td><td>960–1320 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Muscle building</td><td>Maximize synthesis</td><td>1.6–2.2 g</td><td>960–1320 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Athlete</td><td>Performance/recovery</td><td>1.4–2.0 g</td><td>840–1200 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Elderly (50+)</td><td>Prevent sarcopenia</td><td>1.2–1.6 g</td><td>720–960 kcal</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Quick Calculation Method</h3>
  <p>To calculate your protein target:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Know your body weight in kg (or lbs ÷ 2.2)</li>
    <li>Choose your protein multiplier based on goals above</li>
    <li>Multiply: weight × multiplier = grams per day</li>
    <li>Convert to calories: grams × 4 = protein calories</li>
  </ol>
  <p><strong>Example:</strong> 80 kg person wanting muscle growth = 80 × 2.0 = 160g protein = 640 calories from protein.</p>

  <h2 id="best-protein-sources">Best High-Protein Foods (By Calorie Efficiency)</h2>
  <p>These foods give you the most protein for the fewest calories:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Food</th><th scope="col">Protein per 100g</th><th scope="col">Calories per 100g</th><th scope="col">Protein percentage</th><th scope="col">Quality</th></tr></thead>
